{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules","id":535350,"title":"Werewolf Totem List now complete! Updated to include W20 rules!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-01T01:16:08-07:00","id":535350,"title":"Werewolf Totem List now complete! Updated to include W20 rules!","content":"As with the Garou and Fera Gift lists, just follow the link in my signature.<br /> <br /> I went the extra mile and went back and got the Source/page reference for ALL of the Garou totems. I think I included every Garou totem ever published with the exception of Panthilesa from Rage Across the Amazon and Phoenix from the Players Guide(s), but those two are unique totems that can only adopt one pack at a time, so I saw fit not to include them in the list. Fera and Bane totems are also outside the scope of this list, although I *might* do a Fera totem list sometime...but not soon. Between the Gifts lists and this totem list, I'm a bit burned out at the moment.<br /> <br /> In any case, as always, I hope you guys find these lists useful.<br /> <br /> And just for the record, I think Clashing Boom-Boom is the most awesome totem ever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T10:36:13-07:00","id":535713,"title":"","content":"Amazing, thanks. Such a useful resource. (And now I know for sure that there is no premade Crane totem.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:58:56-07:00","id":535977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules?p=535713#post535713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amazing, thanks. Such a useful resource. (And now I know for sure that there is no premade Crane totem.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Crane is not a Garou totem that I can recall, anyway. As to whether it's a Fera totem is at present anyone's guess. I think I very vaguely recall a Crane totem for one of the Fera, but I might be misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T10:22:50-07:00","id":537192,"title":"","content":"Possibly werefoxes or some other fera that has a strong presence in East Asia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T15:07:37-07:00","id":537446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules?p=537192#post537192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly werefoxes or some other fera that has a strong presence in East Asia [have Crane as a totem]?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just went through <i>Hengeyokai </i>and Crane was not listed as a totem. It was interesting to note that some Garou Nation totems, like Chimera, the Wind Incarna and Fox do serve as hengeyokai totems as well. I guess my vague memory of Crane as a totem was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T00:18:42-07:00","id":539329,"title":"","content":"D'OH! Turns out I missed a few things, among them the fact that the Rage Across Appalachia totems are, like the Wendigo Revised totems, not organized according to their totem type. I'm in the process of trying to figure out which category they go. (What the hell was I thinking when I labeled Opposum as a Totem of Wisdom when she's CLEARLY a Cunning Totem???)<br /> <br /> A corrected totems list is forthcoming. Watch this space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T10:17:53-07:00","id":539705,"title":"","content":"One thing I noted, there sure do seem to be a lot of Appalachian-specific totems. Is that region supposed to be a hotbed of werewolf activity or possess some in-game rationale for so many of its spirit animals choosing to become patrons of garou packs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T13:01:59-07:00","id":539867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules?p=539705#post539705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I noted, there sure do seem to be a lot of Appalachian-specific totems. Is that region supposed to be a hotbed of werewolf activity or possess some in-game rationale for so many of its spirit animals choosing to become patrons of garou packs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a 20-year old book, so it might be some form of weirdness from the early days that hasn't yet been revisited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:37:41-07:00","id":540157,"title":"","content":"<i>Rage Across Appalachia</i> had a few Appalachia-specific totems that also functioned as totems for Nunnehi Changelings. <i>Rage Across Appalachia </i>was intended as a crossover supplement for both Werewolf and Changeling in the same vein as <i>Dark Alliance: Vancouver</i> (which we shall not speak of again) or <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i>. The totems listed in there are indeed viable Garou totems, though their packs are rare. Caerns: Places of Power also had a couple of totems which are Asian-locale specific and didn't initially include them in the list for that reason. I just changed my mind, however.<br /> <br /> As of right now (7:36pm EST, June 4, 2015), the Totems List is complete, has all the published Garou totems (minus perhaps a few totems that are only in Changeling: the Dreaming books which I dont have) and are all sourced and cross-referenced. This final version is now available in my signature for download. Here's a useful hint: if your version of the Totems List does not have an Afterword, you've got an incomplete version, so feel free to download the latest version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:58:15-07:00","id":542895,"title":"","content":"D'OH! (x2). I totally forgot to include the totems from White Howlers Tribebook. Cutting and pasting those into the doc file now. Stay tuned.<br /> <br /> EDIT: White Howler totems now added to the doc file. NOW it should be complete (unless there's something *else* I forgot...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:58:26-07:00","id":550766,"title":"","content":"Thank you for such a thing!<br /> It is really useful (i'm making a few edits here and there...but all of this is great!)<br /> <br /> A question: how do you deal with old totems which do not completely respect the new totem model?<br /> E.g. totems which have individual traits but not pack traits?<br /> <br /> My guess is that for most of them one can leave them as they are, with or without either individual or pack traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:42:35-07:00","id":550918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules?p=550766#post550766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for such a thing!<br /> It is really useful (i'm making a few edits here and there...but all of this is great!)<br /> <br /> A question: how do you deal with old totems which do not completely respect the new totem model?<br /> E.g. totems which have individual traits but not pack traits?<br /> <br /> My guess is that for most of them one can leave them as they are, with or without either individual or pack traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alot of it was guesswork. Basically, I compared old totems (without the Individual and Pack Traits) to new totems (that do have the separate Traits), compared the relative Background Costs and tried to extrapolate from there. The text of the totem's traits also gave hints as to what were Pack Traits (which are shared among the pack one individual at a time) and Individual Traits (which each member of the pack all get).<br /> <br /> A rule of thumb is that stuff like Willpower, Gnosis and Rage point pools are almost always Pack Traits as point pools are &quot;owned&quot; by one packmate until he relinquishes the pool to a different packmate. Gifts are usually also a Pack Trait unless the totem has a very high Background Cost or the text specifically states that every member of the pack can access it. Example 1: Hyperion with a Background Cost of 10 and everyone in the pack can use the Level Five Gift: Kiss of Helios <i>regardless of Rank</i>. Example 2: Gallia from White Howlers Tribebook, who has a Background Cost of <i>12 (</i>yes, 12!), and can grant each member of the pack the Level Five Gift: Fabric of the Mind, also regardless of Rank. (When the White Howlers fell, Gallia fell alongside them and became G\u2019louogh, \u201cThe Demon Goddess\u201d, referred to by some as the \u201cmother of all Banes.\u201d Her fall was a great loss to the Garou.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 06-11-2015, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:59:27-07:00","id":657656,"title":"","content":"Thanks for these!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T01:27:35-07:00","id":681843,"title":"","content":"Oh curious on Renown penaltys is the penalty too great when it reduces a lot of rewards to 0? <br /> its a worthwhile thing to note, I think.As I Would like my Philodex of Bat to be able to go up in rank at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T20:00:25-07:00","id":691911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/535350-werewolf-totem-list-now-complete-updated-to-include-w20-rules?p=681843#post681843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I'm curious on Renown penalties: is the penalty too great when it reduces a lot of rewards to 0?<br /> It's a worthwhile thing to note, I think, as I would like my Philodox of Bat to be able to go up in rank at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the penalty reduces a renown award to zero, then it must be a punishment for a severe screwup. I didn't make the rules, I just copied them from their sourcebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T02:10:41-07:00","id":692151,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the totem renown grants and penalties are... odd. Certain totems like Falcon include a tiny one-time boost that is less than what you'd get for even a lower-medium deed. Others, like bear, detract a set number of points from every reward, being potentially irrelevant if you manage a few great deeds, but eating up all your renown if you accumulate it point-by-point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}